From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shahed <jamshidalinezhadian@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0330
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: read the WPA3 SAE feature through isWpa3SaeSupported()

On LineageOS 22.2 (Android 15) getSupportedFeatures() returns a BitSet
instead of a long bitmask, and WifiManager.WIFI_FEATURE_WPA3_SAE is a
bit index. The transition-disable check still masked the old long, so
wifi-service failed to compile:

  ClientModeImpl.java: error: bad operand types for binary operator '&'
    first type:  BitSet
    second type: int

Use the class's existing isWpa3SaeSupported(), which reads the bit
from the BitSet. The behaviour is unchanged.

Change-Id: I4b8e1d6a2c9f3e7a5d0b8c2e6f1a9d3b7c5e0f48
---
 service/java/com/android/server/wifi/ClientModeImpl.java | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/ClientModeImpl.java b/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/ClientModeImpl.java
index 2d35e0b..0fffe57 100644
--- a/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/ClientModeImpl.java
+++ b/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/ClientModeImpl.java
@@ -6025,7 +6025,9 @@ public class ClientModeImpl extends StateMachine implements ClientMode {
                         // after which the network is never handed to wpa_supplicant again
                         // ("No available security params").
                         if ((indication & WifiMonitor.TDI_USE_WPA3_PERSONAL) != 0
-                                && (getSupportedFeatures() & WifiManager.WIFI_FEATURE_WPA3_SAE) == 0) {
+                                // Android 15 returns the feature set as a BitSet; the class's
+                                // own helper reads the WPA3 SAE bit from it.
+                                && !isWpa3SaeSupported()) {
                             log("Ignoring WPA3 Personal transition disable: SAE not supported");
                             indication &= ~WifiMonitor.TDI_USE_WPA3_PERSONAL;
                         }
